# Paths excluded from the nightly /data snapshot (#100).
#
# The rule: exclude what is REPRODUCIBLE or CIRCULAR, never what is merely large.
# Everything not listed here is backed up, including /data/k8s-pv (#103), which
# must be — a k3s persistent volume is a directory on the pet disk and inherits
# this backup set by design.

# Docker's and containerd's storage roots, moved to /data by #99. Image layers
# and snapshots are enormous and are re-pullable from a registry; backing them up
# would inflate the repository for zero recovery value. Container *state* that
# matters lives in a bind mount under /data/<app>, which IS backed up.
/data/docker
/data/containerd

# restic's own cache. Pure derived data, rebuilt on demand, and backing it up
# would grow the repository roughly in proportion to itself.
/data/.cache

# The repository password. Circular — it would be encrypted with itself, so it is
# unreadable exactly when it would be needed — and a restore onto a fresh disk
# should not silently repopulate a credential. Its copies live in the password
# manager and in the secret-files container (R13, docs/runbooks/restic_backup.md).
/data/.restic-password

# ext4 recovery scratch.
/data/lost+found
